  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The three cut layers of `SdfField` (`cuts`, `cut_ups`, `cut_downs`) hold each brick in an `Arc` (`CutLayer`, `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/field.rs`).\n- A clone of the field copies the keys and the pointers only. It shares the bricks.\n- A write goes through `layer_brick_mut` (`Arc::make_mut`). It copies a brick first when a clone still holds that brick.\n- `claim_record` and `up_record` read the cell first. They take the writable brick only when the value changes. A move that changes no cell copies no brick.\n- `KeyCost` has a new method, `key_bytes_after(prev)`. The keyframe store counts a keyframe by the bricks that the keyframe before it does not share, and by its map entries.\n- `Keyframes::offer` and `Keyframes::held_bytes` use that count. The budget, the thinning and the stride law do not change.\n- The public API of the sim crate only grows: `SdfField::cut_bytes_after` and `KeyCost::key_bytes_after` (with a default).\n\n## Cause\n\nA playback keyframe was a whole copy of the cut layers (#2181, PR #2192). Two keyframes one stride apart differ only in the bricks that the moves between them changed. The store paid for all bricks in each keyframe.\n\n## Readings\n\nDense 100 mm face (`precalc_reading_on_the_dense_face`, release, 4268 moves, 68 keyframes, stride 64):\n\n| | Keyframe bytes | Calculation time |\n|---|---|---|\n| `upstream/main` (old sim sources) | 444 940 288 (424 MiB) | 49.8 s |\n| This PR | 65 181 664 (62 MiB) | 30 s to 32 s (three runs) |\n\nThe factor is 6.8. The test asserts a factor of 6 at least.\nThe machine had other builds in progress, so the times are not exact.\n\nStaged 24 mm face at 0.5 mm cells (debug, 28 keyframes): 9 923 808 bytes held. Whole copies cost 45 301 760 bytes. The factor is 4.56. The test asserts a factor of 4 at least.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins:\n\n- `the_keyframes_share_the_bricks_that_no_move_changed` (`crates/app/tests/stock_play_precalc.rs`). It asserts the factor of 4, the equality of the running count and the audit, and the bit-identical replay at six positions.\n- `a_keyframe_costs_what_the_one_before_does_not_share` (`crates/sim/tests/play_keys.rs`). It asserts the count on plain values, before and after a thinning.\n- `a_clone_shares_its_cut_bricks_and_a_write_copies_first` (`crates/sim/tests/play_keys.rs`). It asserts that a clone is not written through, and that the cut over shared bricks is the plain cut, bit for bit.\n- `precalc_reading_on_the_dense_face` (heavy lane, release). It now asserts the factor of 6 on the dense face.\n\nRed before the fix: the first pin failed on unchanged code with `8454144 bytes held; whole copies cost 8454144`.\n\nMutations (each one red, then green after the restore):\n\n- `offer` counts `value.key_bytes()` (the old line): `a_keyframe_costs_what_the_one_before_does_not_share` is red.\n- `held_bytes` sums whole copies (the old line): the same test is red, `(5, 1, 40, 100)` against `(5, 1, 40, 40)`.\n- `layer_brick_mut` writes through the shared pointer: `a_clone_shares_its_cut_bricks_and_a_write_copies_first` is red at \"a shared brick is copied before the write\".\n- `claim_record` takes the writable slot before the read: `the_keyframes_share_the_bricks_that_no_move_changed` is red, `16358624 bytes held; whole copies cost 45301760`.\n- All of `crates/sim/src` from `upstream/main`: `precalc_reading_on_the_dense_face` is red, `444940288 bytes held; whole copies cost 444940288`.\n\nUnchanged and green: `the_precalculated_stock_is_the_live_cut_at_every_position`, `a_live_seek_after_a_cancel_keeps_the_byte_budget`, `the_worker_calculates_first_then_replays_and_the_post_gate_is_unchanged` (the replay is bit-identical, the budget holds, the post gate reads the same).\n\nGate on the final head: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green, 11 steps, 0 failed (sim lib, `play_keys`, `play_precalc`, `stock_carry_side_exact`, `stock_columns`, `stock_field_cost`, `stock_sdf`; app `stock_field_cost`, `stock_play_precalc`). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\nHeavy lanes that ran (release, `--ignored`): app `stock_play_precalc` and app `stock_field_cost`. The two are green.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\" \"*.png\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` plans 217 steps for this diff. Only the two heavy binaries above ran. The other heavy lanes did not run. Run them before this PR is flagged ready.\n- The `camcraft-ui` crate was not built. This PR changes no item that the UI crate can see, other than the two additions.\n- The gate and the tests ran without sccache and with a target directory outside the worktree. The sccache daemon on this machine executed no compile, and a stuck `cargo check` of the editor tooling held the build lock of the worktree.\n- `CostLedger` (the cut region, the full-brick ledger, the dirty set) is still copied whole by each keyframe. The store does not count it, as before.\n- The time of one cell write was not measured alone. The dense face calculation as a whole is faster.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #2714 changes other files in `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/` and `crates/app/src/stock_play.rs`. It changes none of the files of this PR.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/2194-share-keyframe-bricks.md`.\n\nEffort: max\n\nChangelog: Simulation playback: keyframes share the stock bricks that no move changed, so the calculation before playback uses much less memory (the dense 100 mm face: 62 MiB, before 424 MiB) and keeps a shorter stride on large programs.\n\nFixes #2194\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
